    "q-35558": {
      "dom_id": "step-q35558",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Let $W$ be the set of all polynomials in the variable $x\\in R$ with coefficients in $R$ of degree $5$ or greater. Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$W$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to polynomials addition and multiplication of a polynomial by a real number) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*",
      "worked_solution": "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$W$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to polynomials addition and multiplication of a polynomial by a real number) because **$W$ does not contain the zero element.** *\n\nIndeed, the zero polynomial has degree $0$, which is less than $5.$\n\nOn the other hand: \n\n- Addition of polynomials is associative. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition of polynomials is commutative. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition and scalar multiplication of polynomials satisfy the distributive laws. $\\,✓$\n\n- For any polynomial $p(x)$ of degree $5$ (or greater), the corresponding negative polynomial $-p(x)$ has the same degree. $\\,✓$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
