    "q-43858": {
      "dom_id": "step-q43858",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Let $V$ be the set of all  $2\\times 2$ invertible matrices with real entries, with the usual matrix addition and scalar multiplication. Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$V$ is **not** a vector space  because $\\text{____}\\,.$*",
      "worked_solution": "The correct answer is \n\n*$V$ is **not** a vector space  because **the $2\\times 2$ zero matrix is not in $V.$** *\n\nIndeed, the zero matrix doesn't have an inverse, so it doesn't belong to $V.$ As a result, $V$ cannot be a vector space.\n\nOn the other hand, \n\n- Addition of matrices is associative.  $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition of matrices is commutative.  $\\,✓$\n\n- The $2\\times 2$ identity matrix is invertible, so it belongs to $V.$  $\\,✓$\n\n- If $A$ is invertible then $-A$ is invertible too. So, $-A\\in V.$ $\\,✓$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-43858-a",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "If $A\\in V$ then $-A\\notin V$",
              "html": "If <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"120\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D434 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2208\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D449 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> then <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"121\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2212\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D434 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2209\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D449 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi>V</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> \n"
            },
            {
              "option": "b",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-43858-b",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "the $2\\times 2$ identity matrix  is not in $V$",
