    "q-74671": {
      "dom_id": "step-q74671",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\text{A}1]-[\\text{A}8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement: *\n\n*If $x$ is a vector such that $-x+w=w$ for some $w\\in V$, then $x=0$* \n\n*Proof:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-x+w & =w &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ x+(-x+w) & =x+w &  & [\\,\\text{adding }x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (x+(-x))+w & =x+w &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ 0+w & =x+w &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ w & =x+w &  & [\\,\\text{axiom  A3}\\,] \\\\ w+(-w) & =x+w+(-w) &  & [\\,\\text{adding }-w\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ w+(-w) & =x+(w+(-w)) &  & [\\,\\text{axioms  A2}\\,] \\\\ 0 & =x+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,] \\\\ 0 & =x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom  A3}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe axioms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{[A1]}:x+y=y+x & \\text{[A5]}:1\\cdot x=x \\\\ \\text{[A2]}:(x+y)+z=x+(y+z) & \\text{[A6]}:\\alpha (\\beta x)=(\\alpha \\beta )x \\\\ \\text{[A3]}:x+0=x & \\text{[A7]}:(\\alpha +\\beta )x=\\alpha x+\\beta x \\\\ \\text{[A4]}:x+(-x)=0 & \\text{[A8]}:\\alpha (x+y)=\\alpha x+\\alpha y\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the vector space axioms, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-x+w & =w &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ x+(-x+w) & =x+w &  & [\\,\\text{adding }x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (x+(-x))+w & =x+w &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A2}\\,\\,] \\\\ 0+w & =x+w &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ w & =x+w &  & [\\,\\text{axiom  A3}\\,] \\\\ w+(-w) & =x+w+(-w) &  & [\\,\\text{adding }-w\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ w+(-w) & =x+(w+(-w)) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom  A2}\\,] \\\\ 0 & =x+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A4}\\,\\,] \\\\ 0 & =x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom  A3}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
