    "q-106942": {
      "dom_id": "step-q106942",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\text{A}1]-[\\text{A}8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement: *\n\n*If $u$ and $v$ are vectors such that $u+x=v+x$ for some $x\\in V,$ then $u=v.$*\n\n*Proof:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u+x & =v+x &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (u+x)+(-x) & =(v+x)+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ u+(x+(-x)) & =v+(x+(-x)) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A2}\\,] \\\\ u+0 & =v+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ u & =v &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe axioms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{[A1]}:x+y=y+x & \\text{[A5]}:1\\cdot x=x \\\\ \\text{[A2]}:(x+y)+z=x+(y+z) & \\text{[A6]}:\\alpha (\\beta x)=(\\alpha \\beta )x \\\\ \\text{[A3]}:x+0=x & \\text{[A7]}:(\\alpha +\\beta )x=\\alpha x+\\beta x \\\\ \\text{[A4]}:x+(-x)=0 & \\text{[A8]}:\\alpha (x+y)=\\alpha x+\\alpha y\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the vector space axioms, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u+x & =v+x &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (u+x)+(-x) & =(v+x)+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ u+(x+(-x)) & =v+(x+(-x)) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A2}\\,] \\\\ u+0 & =v+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A4}\\,] \\\\ u & =v &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A3}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
