    "q-35629": {
      "dom_id": "step-q35629",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\text{A}1]-[\\text{A}8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement:* \n\n*$\\alpha 0=0$ for any $\\alpha \\in R$*\n\n*Proof:* \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\alpha 0 & =\\alpha 0 &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ \\alpha 0 & =\\alpha (0+0) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A3}\\,] \\\\ \\alpha 0 & =\\alpha 0+\\alpha 0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ \\alpha 0+(-\\alpha 0) & =(\\alpha 0+\\alpha 0)+(-\\alpha 0) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-\\alpha 0\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ \\alpha 0+(-\\alpha 0) & =\\alpha 0+(\\alpha 0+(-\\alpha 0)) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A2}\\,] \\\\ 0 & =\\alpha 0+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ 0 & =\\alpha 0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A3}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe axioms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{[A1]}:x+y=y+x & \\text{[A5]}:1\\cdot x=x \\\\ \\text{[A2]}:(x+y)+z=x+(y+z) & \\text{[A6]}:\\alpha (\\beta x)=(\\alpha \\beta )x \\\\ \\text{[A3]}:x+0=x & \\text{[A7]}:(\\alpha +\\beta )x=\\alpha x+\\beta x \\\\ \\text{[A4]}:x+(-x)=0 & \\text{[A8]}:\\alpha (x+y)=\\alpha x+\\alpha y\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the vector space axioms, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\alpha 0 & =\\alpha 0 &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ \\alpha 0 & =\\alpha (0+0) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A3}\\,] \\\\ \\alpha 0 & =\\alpha 0+\\alpha 0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A8}\\,] \\\\ \\alpha 0-\\alpha 0 & =(\\alpha 0+\\alpha 0)-\\alpha 0 &  & [\\,\\text{add }-\\alpha 0\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ \\alpha 0-\\alpha 0 & =\\alpha 0+(\\alpha 0-\\alpha 0) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A2}\\,] \\\\ 0 & =\\alpha 0+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A4}\\,] \\\\ 0 & =\\alpha 0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A3}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
